# Rust backend rules

- Keep Tauri commands thin; put logic in `services/` or domain modules.
- Use `thiserror` (`AppError`) and map at the command boundary.
- Never build shell strings — always argv arrays for yt-dlp/ffmpeg.
- Validate URLs (http/https only), paths, enums, and lengths.
- Canonicalize paths and reject traversal outside download roots.
- Prefer Tokio for process/network I/O; do not block the main thread.
- Add unit tests for pure validators and template expanders.
